### 2026-08-14T02:13:33.502Z | claude (claude-sonnet-5) | claude | conversation 627637ca-d250-4ad7-8a24-ddd841e171dd

Good catch — that does look like the same 4-cell shape landing twice. Two things stand out from what I've found so far:

1. **I already reproduced a real bug**: pasting 3 [REDACTED_STUDENT] into Gravity via the actual header buttons only landed 1 of 3 — nothing was occupied or out-of-cup, so all 3 should have landed. Still digging into why.
2. Compose has a separate, real gap: paste **does** add the notes internally, but Compose never draws a persistent marker for recorded/pasted notes (only a selection ring for ones you've explicitly selected), and paste doesn't update the note-count display either — so a successful paste looks like nothing happened.

For the duplication in your screenshots — one plausible explanation: paste doesn't clear the clipboard, so if the first click seemed to do nothing (matching the Compose-style "no visible feedback" issue) and you clicked Paste a second time, that would legitimately paste the same shape again, landing on whatever cells were still empty next to the first copy. Does that match what happened — did you click paste more than once for that piece?


